{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:2.35.160","page_type":"section"},"citation":"2.35.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","content_hash":"89e9398efa44b807199c878c2345ac0d3c177db5186ca6edb00e039a34882ee1","heading":"Definitions.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","text":"The following words, terms, and phrases, when used in this article, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:\n“Law enforcement officer” means a sworn law enforcement officer employed by the City of Topeka Police Department.\n“No-knock warrant” means any search warrant issued by a judge of the district court that does not require the law enforcement officer(s) executing the warrant to knock and announce themselves, and their purpose, prior to entering a specified premises.\n“Search warrant” for purposes of this chapter means a legal document authorizing a law enforcement officer to enter and search a specified premises. (Ord. 20249 § 1, 7-21-20.)\nCross References: Definitions generally, TMC 1.10.020 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"33aa859f-279b-55b7-af6c-b7951404f83a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.35.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","content_hash":"888a927473649f74a440526b365309f31775bf7c1b34aaa418a5af4e6d33bb73","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","text":"The following words, terms, and phrases, when used in this article, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"9ff8adce-4881-576e-b64a-fb3502e94c7c"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.35.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","content_hash":"379ae3050d6a30d20ff5fed2aae13729a58319bc1d05ccdfd9bcf63db6e8bf2b","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","text":"“Law enforcement officer” means a sworn law enforcement officer employed by the City of Topeka Police Department.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"87943974-f743-5376-8492-45a28f97b490"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.35.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","content_hash":"0703f68b7d83293b0caaeb023ec2af929f1caeafbfd67896d7834cc1a816fbd6","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.35.160:block:2","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","text":"“No-knock warrant” means any search warrant issued by a judge of the district court that does not require the law enforcement officer(s) executing the warrant to knock and announce themselves, and their purpose, prior to entering a specified premises.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"b587c499-bb6a-58cf-aec6-838155897e93"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.35.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.35.160","content_hash":"cd8884f2a4f1a1550b565002cb939add802